-- title:
--   Smooth-point stalks at all layers from the base layer (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$ (the rigidifying auxiliary level).
--
--   **Reduction data.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$, which by `LiesOverPrime` means that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`. $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $=\kappa(j_q,\,j_{q,M'})$ over $\kappa$ whose members are exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational (the map $\kappa\to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` in the set `ssJSet q κ`; $s$ is an element of $W$. The hypothesis `hle` is an inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of intermediate fields of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: the first is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, the second (written $\bar F$ below) the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of `xHFunctionField (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, that is, the subgroup of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A$ on constants, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of functions with non-zero residue, and the property that every non-zero element can be scaled by a constant into the integers with non-zero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise image of $y$ under the residue map of $A$.
--
--   **Base field and its local data.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$; the ring $A\cap k_0$ (formally `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`) is assumed to be a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, to be a Henselian local ring, and to have algebraically closed residue field; the hypothesis `hκ` says that every $a\in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary parameters.** $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le \ell$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **The tower of layers.** $\iota$ is a type, $K:\iota\to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with each $K_n$ finite over $k_0$, and $A_n$ a valuation subring of $K_n$ cutting out $A$ (for $x\in K_n$: $x\in A_n$ iff $x\in A$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$). In addition a base layer is given: $K_b$ with $K_b=\bot$ (so $K_b$ is $k_0$ itself inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cutting out $A$, and $\varpi_b\ne 0$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Statement.** Equip $\bar F$ with the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\bar F$. The assertion is: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\bar F/k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that
--
--   (G) the join of $k_0(\mathrm{range}\,(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\bar F))$ with $F_0$ is all of $\bar F$, and
--
--   (LD) for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar F$ with all $a_i$ in the join of $k_0(\text{image of }K'\text{ in }\bar F)$ with $F_0$: if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i (c_i\text{ in }\bar F)\,a_i=0$, then $a_i=0$ for all $i$,
--
--   and for every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ that is a $\kappa$-algebra and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $\bar F$ to $\mathrm{FSS}$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of $\bar F$, a surjective residue homomorphism to $\mathrm{FSS}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ on constants, and with the scaling property) such that $F_0\cap R.\mathrm{integers}=W_0$ (for $f\in F_0$: $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ iff $f\in W_0$), the following implication holds between the base-layer package and the all-layers package.
--
--   **Antecedent.** It consists of two conjuncts.
--
--   (D) *Drinfeld identification.* For every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e:\mathrm{FSS}\simeq$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field, inside the Drinfeld function field `FractionRing (CoordRing q κ)`, of the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `hFunctionFieldAction q κ ⟨(1, ζ), _⟩` for $\zeta\in C_s$) such that $\mathrm{card}\,C_s = 2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` — the latter being `jWidthChar q` of the value of $s$ at `jGeomGen κ M'` divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`, so for $q=3$ the numerator is $6$ if that value is $0$ and $1$ otherwise, and the denominator is the non-negative part of the order of vanishing at $s$ of `jGeomGen` minus that value — and such that $e$ is equivariant: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every hypothesis that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers`, and every proof that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,u)\mapsto \det g\cdot u^{q+1}$), the automorphism of $\mathrm{FSS}$ induced by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` through `R.resAut` corresponds under $e$, inside the Drinfeld function field, to `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at that element.
--
--   (B) *Base-layer stalks.* There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$, an assignment $Q\mapsto S_b(Q)$ of subrings of $\bar F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_b(Q):A_b[X]\to S_b(Q)$ and $\chi_b(Q):S_b(Q)\to\kappa$, and sets $D_b(Q)$ of places of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that: $|N|=q+1$;
--
--   *(affine chart)* there is a subring $B$ of $\bar F$ with $B\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $B\subseteq S_b(Q)$ for every $Q\notin N$, and such that every $z\in\mathrm{FSS}$ which lies in the valuation subring of every $Q\notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $B$;
--
--   and for every $Q\notin N$: the image in $\bar F$ of every $a\in A_b$ lies in $S_b(Q)$; $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a)$ has that image as its value in $\bar F$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(X))=0$; $S_b(Q)$ is local with $\ker\chi_b(Q)$ its maximal ideal; $S_b(Q)$ is contained in the join of $k_0(\text{image of }K_b)$ with $F_0$, and conversely every element of that join is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in S_b(Q)$, $h\ne 0$; $\varphi_b(Q)$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; all elements of $S_b(Q)$ lie in `R.integers`, and such an element lies in the maximal ideal of `R.integers` exactly when it is divisible by $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,\varpi_b)$ in $S_b(Q)$; for every $f\in S_b(Q)$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi_b(Q)(f)$ under $\kappa\to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_b(Q)(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; and $D_b(Q)$ consists exactly of the places $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that are rational, for which every $f\in S_b(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and for which, for every $f\in S_b(Q)$, the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $<1$ if and only if $\chi_b(Q)(f)=0$.
--
--   Furthermore: for $Q,Q'\notin N$, a place $P$ belonging to both $D_b(Q)$ and $D_b(Q')$ forces $Q=Q'$; for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_b(Q)$ the order of $P$ at the image in $\bar F$, via `hle`, of the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular function $j$ is $\ge 0$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every hypothesis that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, the induced automorphism `R.resAut τ` of $\mathrm{FSS}$ satisfies: $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q\in N$ iff $Q\in N$, and for $Q\notin N$ one has `smulDisc τ (Db Q)` $=D_b(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q)$, where `smulDisc τ D` is the set of places $P$ with $\tau^{-1}\cdot P\in D$.
--
--   **Consequent.** The first conjunct is the clause (D) above, repeated verbatim. The second conjunct asserts the existence of a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$, subrings $S_n(Q,n)$ of $\bar F$ indexed by places $Q$ and layers $n\in\iota$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_n(Q,n):A_n[X]\to S_n(Q,n)$ and $\chi_n(Q,n):S_n(Q,n)\to\kappa$, and sets $D_n(Q,n)$ of places of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that $|N|=q+1$ and:
--
--   *(affine chart)* there is a subring $B$ of $\bar F$ with $B\subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $B\subseteq S_n(Q,n)$ for all $Q\notin N$ and all $n$, and such that every $z\in\mathrm{FSS}$ lying in the valuation subring of every $Q\notin N$ is the $R$-residue of an element of $B$;
--
--   and for every $Q\notin N$ the following hold. First, for every $n\in\iota$: the map $A_n\to\kappa$ induced by the residue map of $A$ is surjective; the image in $\bar F$ of every $a\in A_n$ lies in $S_n(Q,n)$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a)$ has as value in $\bar F$ the image of $a$; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X))=0$; for every $c\in A_n$ with residue $0$ in $\kappa$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi:S_n(Q,n)\to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a))=a$ for all $a\in A_n$, with residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X))=c$; for every $f\in S_n(Q,n)$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; $D_n(Q,n)$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that every $f\in S_n(Q,n)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and such that for every $f$ the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $<1$ iff $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)=0$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ differs from $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,c)$ for every $c\in A_n$; $S_n(Q,n)$ is local with maximal ideal the set of $f$ with $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)=0$, is Noetherian and is a unique factorisation monoid; $S_n(Q,n)$ is contained in the join of $k_0(\text{image of }K_n)$ with $F_0$, and every element of that join is a quotient of elements of $S_n(Q,n)$ with non-zero denominator; the linear disjointness clause (LD) holds for $K_n$ (for every $m$, every $K_n$-linearly independent $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $a$ with values in that join, $\sum_i (c_i\text{ in }\bar F)\,a_i=0$ implies all $a_i=0$); every ring homomorphism $\chi:S_n(Q,n)\to A_n$ splitting the constants and compatible with residues has kernel the principal ideal generated by $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)-\varphi_n(Q,n)(C(\chi(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X))))$; there is a generator $\varpi\ne0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$ such that $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_n(Q,n)$, such that an element $f$ of the join of $k_0(\text{image of }K_n)$ with $F_0$ lies in `R.integers` precisely when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in S_n(Q,n)$ and $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)\nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ not associated to $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x\in S_n(Q,n)$ there is a monic polynomial $r$ over $A_n$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ mapped along $\varphi_n(Q,n)\circ C$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ such that every $f\in S_n(Q,n)$ can be written $f\,h=g$ with $g,h$ in the subring of $\bar F$ generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and with $h$ the image of a unit of $S_n(Q,n)$.
--
--   Second, for this same $Q$ there is a monotonicity witness: whenever $K_n\le K_{n'}$ one has $S_n(Q,n)\subseteq S_n(Q,n')$, and moreover $S_n(Q,n')$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_n(Q,n)$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$; the elements $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ have one and the same image in $\bar F$ for all $n$; and $\chi_n(Q,n')$ restricted along the inclusion $S_n(Q,n)\subseteq S_n(Q,n')$ agrees with $\chi_n(Q,n)$.
--
--   Finally: for $Q,Q'\notin N$, any layer $n$ and any place $P$ lying in both $D_n(Q,n)$ and $D_n(Q',n)$, one has $Q=Q'$; for $Q\notin N$, every $n$ and every $P\in D_n(Q,n)$, the order of $P$ at the image in $\bar F$, via `hle`, of the coefficientwise image of `jq` is $\ge0$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves `R.integers`, and every place $Q$: $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q\in N$ iff $Q\in N$, and if $Q\notin N$ then `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)` $=D_n(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q,\,n)$ for every $n$.
--
--   This is the functorial transfer step in the construction of the smooth-point charts on the supersingular components of the semistable model at the auxiliary level $q^2M'$ with $q=3$: it upgrades a package of chart data over the base layer $k_0$, together with the Drinfeld identification of the special-fibre function field, to the analogous package over every finite layer $K_n$ of the tower, with the monotonicity and residue-compatibility relations between layers. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_three_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_three_of_dvd_affineChart), where the resulting all-layer data, including the affine chart $B$, feed the description of the supersingular part of the special fibre.
